      "reason": "The task directly compares CMIP6 `dissic`, `talk`, and `ph` with GLODAP TCO2, TAlk, and pH, so the variable definitions and the fact that CMIP6 pH is in-situ on the TOTAL scale must be respected.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compare `ph` only with an observational pH on the total scale at in-situ temperature and pressure; among GLODAP pH fields, use the in-situ one (`pHtsinsitutp`), not `pHts25p0`.",
        "`dissic` is DIC and `talk` is total alkalinity including carbonate, nitrogen, silicate, and borate components; note in the answer that the CESM2 paper does not document its carbonate constants if interpretation depends on them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
