      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The requested model-vs-GLODAP comparison for DIC and alkalinity is in micromoles per kilogram, but CMIP6 `dissic` and `talk` are stored per unit volume while GLODAP is per unit mass, so unit conversion is a required computation step.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert model `dissic` and `talk` from per volume to per mass before any comparison to GLODAP: `µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ`, using the in-situ density field from `thetao` and `so` (`compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`), not the default constant density.",
        "For the requested absolute means, biases, RMSE, and depthwise biases, do not compare per-volume and per-mass concentrations directly; state which density was used (`attrs['density_assumption']`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The requested map bias, RMSE, correlation, and depth-wise bias all require comparing model and GLODAP only where both are defined, and ranking models cell-by-cell should use a common mask on the comparison grid.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "For the 1° map comparison, regrid all model fields to the GLODAP 1° grid, then build one shared mask over GLODAP and all three models with `build_comparison_mask`, apply it with `.where(mask)` to every model and GLODAP map, and use that one sample for all model rankings and map metrics.",
        "Because the reference is GLODAP, not WOA23, pass `ocean_only=False` to `build_comparison_mask`; report the cell counts from the mask alongside the map metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The workflow mixes global means/integrals and map comparisons, so means over each source should be computed on native grids while regridding is appropriate only for the requested GLODAP-grid map comparisons.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute each source's own global 0-50 m means and period changes on its native grid with its own weights; regrid to the GLODAP 1° grid only for the cell-by-cell map metrics and the depthwise bias maps/profile.",
        "For biases at 0, 100, 500, 1000 and 2000 m, interpolate each product to those depths with `regrid_vertical` before comparison; do not use nearest model levels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The requested global 0–50 m means from `dissic`, `talk`, `ph`, and depth profiles need correct area/volume weighting over all relevant ocean cells rather than unweighted cell averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "For any 0-50 m global mean of `dissic`, `talk`, or `ph`, use a weighted mean on each source's own grid: `Σ field · volcello / Σ volcello` over valid 0-50 m ocean cells; weights must be masked to the same valid cells as the field.",
        "For regridded map metrics, use area weighting for bias/RMSE/correlation (`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cf-cell-methods",
